  "A last-minute \"Digital Omnibus on AI,\" signed by EU lawmakers on July 8, 2026, splits the AI Act's compliance calendar into two speeds: transparency duties such as chatbot disclosure, deepfake labeling, and synthetic-content watermarking still take effect on August 2, 2026, but the heavier high-risk-system obligations are pushed back roughly seventeen months, to December 2027 or later. The same package quietly adds a new ban on AI tools that generate non-consensual intimate imagery and hands the EU's AI Office broader oversight of vertically integrated frontier labs.": "O le 'Digital Omnibus on AI' na sainia e le Palemene o le EU i le aso 8 Iulai 2026, i se taimi tuai, e vaevaeina ai le kalena o le usita'ia o le AI Act i saoasaoa e lua: o matafaioi fa'amanino e pei o le fa'ailoaina o chatbot, fa'ailogaina o deepfake, ma le fa'ailogaina o anotusi fatu (synthetic content) o lo'o amata pea ona fa'amalosia i le aso 2 Aokuso 2026, ae o matafaioi mamafa mo faiga a'afia tele ua tolopo mo le tusa ma le sefululu masina, e o'o atu i Tesema 2027 pe mulimuli atu ai. O le fa'aputuga lava e tasi ua fa'aopoopo lemu ai se fa'asaina fou i meafaigaluega AI e fatuina ata o le tino e le'i malie ai le tagata, ma tu'uina atu i le Ofisa AI a le EU se va'aiga lautele atili o fale su'esu'e maualuluga ua tu'ufa'atasia fa'apogaimoana.",
