  "AI content payment is not merely a copyright or transaction-efficiency problem; it is a question of political-economic legitimacy. As AI valuations reach hundreds of billions, society asks why the gains from public web content and human knowledge accrue to a few firms. The paper proposes a six-layer tiered data market — from free public content through scarce verified datasets to public benefit-sharing — and defines the AI network democratic economy: rights, pricing, participation, auditability, and returns, each democratized through machine-readable protocols like AICR/AICL.": "O le totogiga mo anotusi AI e le na'o se fa'afitauli o aia tusitusi po'o le lelei o fefa'ataua'iga; o se fesili lea e uiga i le fa'amaoni fa'aleaganu'u-fa'apolokiki. A'o o'o atu tau o le AI i le faitau selau piliona, e fesili sosaiete pe aisea e maua ai fua o anotusi lautele o le uepi ma le poto faaletagata e na'o ni kamupani e to'aitiiti. E fautuaina e le pepa se maketi fa'avasega e ono vaega — mai anotusi lautele fua e o'o atu i seti fa'amaumauga fa'amaonia e le tele, se'ia o'o i le fa'asoaina o aoga lautele — ma fa'amatalaina ai le tamaoaiga fa'apulapula fa'aupega o le AI: aia tatau, tau, auai, mafai ona iloilo, ma tupe maua, e fa'apulapulaina ta'itasi e ala i protokolo e mafai ona faitauina e masini e pei o le AICR/AICL.",
